WEBVTT

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:46.580
It looks like we are out of the worst-case scenario.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:58.590
Either the Imperials’ morale have started to fall, or maybe the Gallian soldiers are excelling.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:06.600
That son of Gunther... his evaluation within the military has risen as well.

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.070
I don't like it.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:17.880
Raising our morale is necessary, but why does the militia have to be the symbol of it?

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.510
It's just easy to understand.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:24.290
Besides, "son of a hero" has a good ring to it.

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.790
Hmph. That is just a fantasy.

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:32.990
The war from here on is going to be those of highly-educated professionals.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.980
We have no need for a layman.

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:40.190
A hero is needed by none other than us Regulars.

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:45.830
Then it would be wise to give our layman hero a quick exit.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:51.060
I suggest that we choose this position for the militia’s next target of action.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.820
Fouzen, huh?

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.020
It seems like a fitting place for their grave.

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:05.620
Chapter 13

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:05.620
Moving Fortress of Horror

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:09.130
Fouzen, of all places, huh?

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:11.080
This is some bad luck.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.740
C'mon. Don't say that.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.100
We are one of the luckier ones.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:20.670
But Commander, whether or not we are the bait, this is Fouzen, you know?

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:22.430
There is no change in the harshness.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.020
You're right on that one.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.090
Whatever. Let's get rolling.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:32.280
All right. Let's get this show on the road!

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:37.090
Let's give those who jump into the ogre's lair a tribute of fireworks!

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:40.120
Squad 5, march forward!

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.520
What?!

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:53.470
Can it be?

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:54.270
It's here!

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:10.140
There it goes.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:15.590
The military sure had some nerve to execute this kind of operation.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:20.920
Whatever the higher-ups think, we have no need to know, huh?

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.040
Okay. Let's get going.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.980
Everyone, time to move.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.450
Why do I have to take part in this?

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.870
It is a very reckless operation,

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:42.660
but, I understand that they want to take back Fouzen even by such means.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:48.620
Fouzen is an industrial city that produces a prominent amount of Gallia's ragnite.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:54.930
Depending on who is controlling this city, the tide of war from here on could change greatly.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:57.450
Is that what it is, Welkin?

00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:00.410
Huh? Yeah.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:06.400
If I told you I like Alicia, then what would you do?

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:14.750
Dammit!

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:17.400
Why do we have to act like some guerrillas?

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:21.030
It is impossible to take out that weapon with a frontal attack.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.650
I think that's what headquarters decided.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:26.260
But then why'd it have to be us?

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:29.860
No matter who, somebody has to do it.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:37.510
Those damn Imps, bringing their crazy machinery!

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:32.620
Twenty 'til the next projectile loading!

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:37.410
All units! Get in your defensive positions, and commence preparations for the pursuit!

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:38.230
Hmph.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:40.340
Gallian weaklings.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:46.300
No matter how many forces you muster, I won’t let Fouzen fall into your hands.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:50.670
No, you can't even get close to here.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:55.860
Commander, how much loss do you think we will suffer?

00:05:55.860 --> 00:06:00.130
I don't know. We aren't going to lose anything however.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:06.700
In theory, Fouzen is not geographically fit for a defensive, but...

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:12.340
Thanks to that armored locomotive, this city has been turned into an impregnable fortress.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:21.900
With that artillery piece having an unbelievable range, it is able to perform one-sided attacks.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.490
We can't even get close to it.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:32.010
But even so, an operation that makes us assault an enemy point without even a tank?

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:35.040
The higher-ups are definitely corrupt.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.460
However, it is worth a try.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:42.140
Even the Imperials won't think those troops would be anything more than a decoy.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:50.110
To make the sacrifices of our comrades worth it, we have to infiltrate the city, no matter what.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:54.320
Enemy forces are on the run.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:57.920
Splendid show, General Gregor, sir.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.800
Don't say such a stupid thing.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.880
You call this an operation?

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:07.040
Even a child could carry this out.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:13.130
This was all done because of the geography of Fouzen and the Armed Locomotive “Esen.”

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:38.850
It's here.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:47.100
Quite a preparation there.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.880
That's Fouzen's Resistance for you.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:51.250
Resistance?

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:55.010
Seems like it was formed after the fall of the city.

00:07:57.880 --> 00:08:01.190
Out of all things, I never thought I would come to this city.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:05.050
When we come into contact with them, we will seek their cooperation.

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.440
Everyone, keep that in mind.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:10.690
That is, if we are able to get into the town safely.

00:08:56.270 --> 00:08:59.100
It ain’t a ragnite mine for nothing, I see.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:02.040
No need for lighting, huh?

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:02.680
Hm?

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:26.620
It's our guides.

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:37.550
I welcome you, members of the militia.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:41.820
I am Zaka, leader of the resistance movement.

00:09:41.820 --> 00:09:43.290
A Darcsen?!

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:51.960
Squad 1 Commander, Faldio Landzaat.

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:56.960
Squad 7 Commander, Welkin Gunther. Nice to work with you.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:58.720
Yeah, same here.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:01.170
I'll lead you to our base of operations first.

00:10:01.460 --> 00:10:02.920
Follow me.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:15.770
Is there something on my face?

00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:17.010
No.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:20.580
It's just that the smell bothers me.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:21.990
Smell?

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:25.590
I've had problems with the smell of Darcsen for a long time.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:29.640
If I see them lingering before my eyes, I get disgusted.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:31.100
Stop it, Rosie.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.600
I'm not going to!

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:34.640
You knew it was coming!

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:37.760
You knew that if you brought me here, this was going to happen.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:38.940
Rosie.

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:41.940
Too bad, but I can't back down on this one.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:45.160
That's how I have lived up to now.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:52.460
So you think you've become a good human because of that?

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.220
Huh?

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:55.230
We are used to discrimination.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:59.120
I don't care what you think of us,

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:01.260
but keep this in mind:

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:04.060
this is our city,

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:08.940
no matter what you want to do, you'll need our help.

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:11.650
Stop it.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:25.030
Geez, you don't have to take it all out and throw it at them.

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:26.500
Shut up.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:29.310
You came here knowing this will happen.

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:31.250
It isn't race that decides a...

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:33.740
Didn't you hear me when I said "Shut up?"

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:36.450
Well, darn me.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:45.790
Hey, Largo.

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:46.450
Huh?

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:49.960
Why do you think we got chosen for this operation?

00:11:51.550 --> 00:11:52.770
I don't know.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.490
The city seems lonesome for some reason.

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:04.620
Ever since the Empire captured it, it's been like this.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:11.090
People have lost their old vitality, and people have started walking with their eyes planted on the ground.

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:14.090
And the thing that changed the most...

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:15.170
is that.

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:18.460
What's that?

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.580
The symbol of Imperial rule...

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:24.960
The Darcsen concentration camp.

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:33.370
Darcsens from all over are gathered here and are being forced to work.

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:38.160
They're not just from this nation. There seem to be some brought from the Empire as well.

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:41.120
Just because they are Darcsen.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:50.010
We are going to bust that facility and take this town back from the Empire.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:54.350
We have continued fighting for that reason.

00:12:56.390 --> 00:13:00.690
Thanks to that, we were able to make it to this city.

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:03.530
Our interests met each other's.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:06.050
It's time for a briefing.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:08.310
Zaka, join us as well.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:09.490
Sure.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:25.170
We will now begin our briefing.

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:29.630
First of all, I want to thank the Resistance.

00:13:29.630 --> 00:13:33.300
It was all thanks to you that we were able to get into the city safely.

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:40.470
Then, I want to tell all of you beforehand that what we are trying to do will bring about significant chaos.

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:43.340
I will now explain the operation.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:51.210
We militias, Squad 1 and Squad 7, have set three objectives in this operation.

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:58.070
First is here: destruction of armored locomotive "Esen," the greatest obstacle to capturing Fouzen.

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:03.640
Second is here: assault on the mining base which is serving as the enemy's command center.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:08.300
Third is here: liberation of Darcsen concentration camp.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:09.890
The operation begins at late night,

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:14.830
at 0200, we will divide into three teams and carry out the objectives separately.

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:20.920
The leader of Team A, whose objective is to free the concentration camp, is Largo.

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:28.410
The leader of Team B, whose objective is to support Team A and destroy the armored locomotive, is Rosie.

00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:34.630
Team C’s objective is to assault the command center and serve as a decoy.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:38.740
All remaining members will be put under Team C.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:43.930
I will leave the positioning of the Resistance’s people to you, Zaka.

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:44.860
Got it.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:46.870
That is all.

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:48.240
Any questions?

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:51.810
What are the priorities on the objectives?

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:55.250
You can't be thinking that everything will go well.

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:57.900
Of course, the top priority is the armored locomotive.

00:14:58.180 --> 00:15:04.880
You can view the assault on the base and attempt on freeing the concentration camp as decoys, if you wish.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:12.460
Making the enemy believe that this is just another riot put up by the Resistance will be favorable to us as well.

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:20.140
The Regulars plan to begin their assault as soon as the destruction of the armored locomotive is confirmed.

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:25.590
I think that the actual liberation of Fouzen will come after that.

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:30.150
Therefore, that means that we were being used as pawns by the Regulars.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:32.450
Such a thing is trivial.

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:35.440
There is a meaning behind this operation.

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:41.280
No matter what reason the Empire may have, what they are doing is wrong.

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:46.350
To discriminate people because of their race is something that must not go unpunished.

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:49.630
So let us fulfill our mission to the last.

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.760
Yes, that's right.

00:15:52.370 --> 00:15:53.610
Let's do this!

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:54.820
Yeah!

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:57.210
The operation starts in the depth of night.

00:15:57.210 --> 00:16:03.240
Those who are under Team B, take utmost care to learn the city's infrastructures inside out.

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:06.900
Then it's okay for me to go outside, right?

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.160
Yes. You are approved.

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.290
However, there is one condition.

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:26.920
Why, out of all people, are you tagged along with me?

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:28.580
I have already told you.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:33.230
Without us, you guys can't do anything in this town.

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:37.120
Hmph. Do whatever you want.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:44.490
Do you think anyone would look after a wild girl for fun?

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:07.790
Mama!

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:12.120
You have to stay close to me.

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:13.490
Let's go.

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:14.350
Okay.

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:26.310
Keep quiet.

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:34.240
It's all good, I'll pay you well.

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:36.860
Give me some more.

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:38.450
Good grief.

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:40.710
Things sure are heating up there.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:49.920
Ouch.

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:53.340
I don't think that's what you do to your lifesaver.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:56.270
I'm no cheap woman!

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:59.360
You are a woman.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:00.860
What?!

00:18:00.860 --> 00:18:05.610
You're not in the position to say anything.

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:08.540
Discrimination is your patent specialty.

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:21.480
I told you before that while I was on leave for injury, I took a trip back to the ruins.

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:24.860
After I got back, Ramal was all angry at me.

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:29.960
He seemed to have thought that I was with Welkin and searched all over the place.

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:34.870
Heh. That sounds like some tank.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:37.200
I want to get to ride on it some time.

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:40.100
But the feel of the drive isn't so comfy.

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:05.180
Are you guys ready yet?

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:08.660
Why are you coming here?

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:12.290
I found some interest in you.

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:16.690
That's quite an embrace I had. Now, I have to protect you.

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:18.470
Don't make a fool of me!

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:21.820
Good punch there.

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:26.280
Let me tell you one thing.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:30.520
Before a woman, I am a soldier of the militia.

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:32.150
Is that so?

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:35.110
I can smell it.

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:39.640
You're more human than anyone else.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:40.720
What are you saying?

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:46.810
It's time.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:54.140
Okay. Let's go.

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:55.450
Our mission begins.

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:15.640
My name is Brigitte Stark. My friends call me Rosie.

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:24.410
Hey, have you ever thought "Is this right or not?" when you had to make a decision?

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.890
Or wonder, "When will I know?"

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:33.460
Next on Valkyria Chronicles: Chapter 14 – Choices at Fouzen

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:39.550
That longing voice, moisten the lands that have become barren.

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:40.040
Chapter 14

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:40.040
Choices at Fouzen
